    "inscriptions": [
      {
        "inscription": "Artist's title on frontispiece, colophon with 6 poems, and 7 seals: \n[seal] Ch'ien-k'un i ts'ao t'ing. Snow Coloring the World White. Huang-shan lao-jen, Jo-chen, at the age of seventy eight. [2 seals] Fa yin Jo-chen; Huang-shih shih. \n\n(Artist's poems are not translated.)\n\n\tIn the first month of the keng-wu year [1690], I was seventy-eight years old. On a snowy day I was pleased to have my good son-in-law Ch'eng-ssu and other gentlemen visiting me at my Tz'u-ching Hall at Yellow Hill. I did this snowscape to record the event. [2 seals] Fa Jo-chen; Tun Chai. [2 seals at end of painting] Fa yin Jo-chen; Huang-shih shih.\n\n(Translated by Ling-yün (Nora) Shih Liu and Wai-Kam Ho)",
        "inscription_translation": null,
        "inscription_remark": null,
        "sortorder": null
      },
      {
        "inscription": "12 additional seals: 8 of Ho Kuan-wu (20th c.); 1 of Wang Nan-p'ing (20th c.); 3 unidentified.",
